            "review_title": "Review at L'Etoile",
            "review_text": "Vi T\n8 contributions\n0\nCame excited, but left disappointed\nSep 2017 • Couples\nnice decoration, price was very affordable, so we were quite excited placing our order. We waited 40 mnts and nothing were served except drinks while the rest of tables came later but were already served. We asked the waiter but he brushed us off coldly, saying they were very crowded so please wait patiently. Until I could not wait anymore, I stood up and asked the one at counter, turned out they forgot / missed our order. I'm not the type to wanted to make a fuss and was very hungry at that time, so I waited for food. grilled chicken was okay, taste not so fantastic but I finished because i was hungry, but the worst part is their onion soup. The cheese was too chewy and thick, tasted aweful. Or French onion soup supposed to be that way i'm not sure. But other French restaurant that I visited didn't serve this kind of onion soup, not even the buffet ones. We ended up left before dessert were served. I took too long. So i didn't know how good is their dessert.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 3, 2017",
