            "review_title": "Review at L'Etoile",
            "review_text": "Xuan Nguyen\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam143 contributions\n0\nOne of those places where time stand still\nSep 2017 • Solo\nL'etoile nests in a small alley, just off the main street. It's one of those places where you walk in and feel immersed in history. A reminder of the old time.\n\nThey have quite an extensive menu, but the chicken is what they got its name for. \"Cheap eats\" for French food, as you can have a portion of 1 drumstick and a side salad for less than 100k. \n\nIt's not so much about the food (let's face it) - but there are not many places in this busy city where you can sit down on a rainy Sunday, eat a meal that doesn't break your bank, and feel completely at peace... with a hint of nostalgia.\nRead more\nWritten September 24, 2017",
