            "review_text": "Kevin W Chan\nKuala Lumpur, Malaysia305 contributions\n0\nNot this L'Etoile! I went to the WRONG ONE!!!\nJan 2016\nL’Etoile Bistro:\nI had a bad experience at the restaurant branch at Ton That Dam Street in District 1, HCMC!\n(BEWARE: I was told there are many restaurants named L'Etoile in Ho Chi Minh City – so DON’T BE FOOL by the imitations! (L'Etoile at 180Bis Alley Hai Ba Trung Street is the original one, the only one without branches!) - Too bad I went to the imitate one, for TWICE!!!)\nAt first we tried out the 3rd outlet of this restaurant when it first opened a few months back (The other 2 branches located in District 7 and District 3!) – and that alone was a very below average experience: The service was slow, the food was average, and the atmosphere was noisy!\nOK, then I was thinking: Might as well give it a 2nd chance - and today I had lunch there - not many locals (as expected) - only two tables with European travelers.\nI tried my best to give it a fair judgement - okay, the table cloth is nice, the deco is very European feel - but the ambience is Not!\nFirst: It was very noisy! Not from the crowd - BUT FROM THE STAFF behind the counter! They laughed out loud as if no customers were inside the restaurant! How could this be allowed in a 'French Theme' restaurant???? I can see a couple of European customers shaking their head as they left the restaurant after paying.\nSecond: I ordered their Australian steak - okay, the presentation is beautiful (to be fair) --- BUT it was tasteless. I mean it, it was as if I was chewing on a rubber!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\nOverall, I would say, I will not give it a 3rd attempt. I had tried twice, and that was it!\nBrave yourself if you would wanna give it a try! GOOD LUCK! (And I wonder how can this restaurant managed to survive for so many years???)\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 18, 2016",
