            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nAverage chicken, Bad lamb, Weird service.\nOct 2014 • Family\nWe went to the branch at Nguyen Duc Canh, in Phu My Hung estate in District 7.\n\nThe chicken was ok, crispy on the outside. But the portions and display has the quality of a roadside stall, not a restaurant. See picture.\n\nThe lamb shank was a joke. There were just 3 pieces of 2cm*3cm*0.5cm to eat. And they were so overcooked that the meat was dry. How can this be considered lamb shank? And they charged us 15usd for it. We felt cheated.\n\nWe asked to speak to the chef, who refused to come out and instead sent the poor young service girl to tell us that it was their supplier's fault to provide such small lamb shanks, not theirs.\n\nAnother weird thing is that another service staff kept swatting mosquitos with those electric bats... very close to our infant. What was she thinking?!? And that also means the restaurant has many mosquitos.\n\nWe will not go back there again.\nRead more\nWritten November 1, 2014",
